meta {
  name: Create Workflow Step (Cal.eu Booking)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/workflows/{{workflow_id}}/steps
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Reserver sur Cal.eu",
    "step_type": "api_call",
    "order": 1,
    "configuration": {
      "url": "https://api.cal.eu/v2/bookings",
      "method": "POST",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "%env(CAL_EU_API_KEY)%",
        "cal-api-version": "2024-08-13",
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
      },
      "data": {
        "eventTypeId": 369376,
        "start": "{{start_time}}",
        "attendee": {
          "name": "{{attendee_name}}",
          "email": "{{attendee_email}}",
          "timeZone": "Europe/Paris"
        },
        "bookingFieldsResponses": {
          "notes": "{{objet}}"
        }
      }
    },
    "is_active": true
  }
}

docs {
  Second step of the "planifier_entretien" workflow, runs after "Notifier
  Maxime" (order 0) -- the actual booking call the workflow is named for,
  referenced throughout docs/BACKLOG.md but missing from this collection
  until now (the original row's real config was lost in a DB reset and
  never recovered).

  Rebuilt and VERIFIED FOR REAL against Maxime's real Cal.eu account
  (`CAL_EU_API_KEY` in backend/.env) -- GET https://api.cal.eu/v2/me
  (account: maximejolivet, Europe/Paris), GET
  https://api.cal.eu/v2/event-types?username=maximejolivet (eventTypeId
  369376, slug "pro", "Rendez-vous professionnel", 30/60 min, Google Meet),
  and a real POST /v2/bookings via "Test Workflow" that created a real
  booking (id 1367960, 2026-09-01 13:00-14:00 UTC, real Google Meet link).
  `api.cal.eu` is a real, live, Cal.com-API-compatible service (identical
  response envelope/error shapes to Cal.com's own v2 API) -- NEVER assume
  it's interchangeable with api.cal.com without checking, they are
  different accounts/keys.

  Two real bugs found and fixed while getting that booking to succeed:
  - `Authorization` header must be EXACTLY `%env(VAR)%`, no prefix/suffix --
    WorkflowExecutionService::resolveEnvHeaders() anchors its regex
    (`^%env\(\w+\)%$`), so a value like `"Bearer %env(CAL_EU_API_KEY)%"`
    silently fails to substitute and sends that literal string as the
    header (401, not an error the code surfaces distinctly from a real
    invalid key). Fix used here: put the full `"Bearer <key>"` string
    *inside* `CAL_EU_API_KEY` itself in backend/.env, keep the header value
    as the bare placeholder.
  - The messenger worker container only reads backend/.env at process
    boot -- adding/editing a var there needs `docker restart
    backend_symfony-worker-1` (or equivalent) before an async step picks it
    up; the app/php-fpm container re-reads per-request so doesn't need this
    for synchronous paths, only this worker.

  `objet` -> `bookingFieldsResponses.notes` wiring is verified live (real
  booking id 1368010 landed with the right `notes`/`description`).

  Placeholders here are `{{start_time}}`/`{{attendee_name}}`/
  `{{attendee_email}}`/`{{objet}}`, matching Workflow.parametersSchema --
  NOT `{{date_souhaitee}}`/`{{nom}}`/`{{prenom}}`/`{{contact_email}}` (an
  earlier version of this step and schema, briefly live, broke
  MessageBubble.vue's "Entretien confirme" card because it reads exactly
  `args.start_time`/`args.attendee_name` -- see "Create Workflow"'s docs
  block for the full explanation). If you ever change these field names
  again, update the frontend's `bookingConfirmation` computed in
  MessageBubble.vue in the same change, not just this step/schema.
}
